<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="850" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112196" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15.jpeg 1264w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-296x300.jpeg 296w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-1011x1024.jpeg 1011w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-768x778.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>In 2013, I got tired of <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2013/01/18/books-emacs-and-isbn-apis/">rooting through the book cases</a> every time I bought a new book (to see whether I already had it, because who can remember those things).  </p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112194" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-300x200.jpg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-768x512.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/DSC01782-2048x1365.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>So I bought an ISBN bar scanner, and whipped up some basic code in Emacs to keep track of what I&#8217;d bought.  I&#8217;ve used it for over a decade now, and it works fine, but it&#8217;s super duper basic:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="687" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112174" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14.jpeg 1376w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-300x246.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1024x839.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-768x629.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>It&#8217;s basically just a buffer that lists all the authors, and then if you click them, you get:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="481" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112175" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1.jpeg 1288w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1-300x172.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1-1024x587.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-1-768x440.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>A list of all the books from that author, as well as the registered publication date.</p>
<p>So that&#8217;s fine, but:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-2.jpeg" alt="" width="694" height="174" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112179" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-2.jpeg 694w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-14-2-300x75.jpeg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 694px) 100vw, 694px" /></a></p>
<p>The data quality from the various ISBN lookup providers is pretty bad.  I mean, it&#8217;s not only the inconsistency, but it&#8217;s also sometimes altogether wrong, because ISBN reuse is a thing, unfortunately.</p>
<p>In addition, I&#8217;ve been buying ebooks too, and these are totally outside this system.  Whenever I buy a papery physical book, I blitz it with the bar code scanner, and it&#8217;s registered &#8212; it takes me literally two seconds or less.  With ebooks, I&#8217;ve got no system at all, and I&#8217;m buying via three different online stores, so my book shopping headache has reestablished itself.</p>
<p>So I hear what you&#8217;re saying: Just bite the bullet and use Librarything for everything.  And I say: No!  So there!  <em>stomps foot</em></p>
<p>Voila!</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-1.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-1.jpeg" alt="" width="393" height="85" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112197" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-1.jpeg 393w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-1-300x65.jpeg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 393px) 100vw, 393px" /></a></p>
<p>I spent one day tinkering with this thing, and now I can edit the data to satisfy my CDO (it&#8217;s like OCD, only the letters are in the proper alphabetical order), and I can add ebooks (manually-ish, <em>sigh</em>).  When the data is easily available like this, the obvious errors (like with the author name above) can be fixed very quickly.  </p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="783" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112198" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2.jpeg 1379w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2-300x280.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2-1024x956.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-2-768x717.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I added more support to the <tt>isbn.el</tt> library to do Goodreads queries, too.  Goodreads doesn&#8217;t have an API any more, so I have to do some web scraping, which sucks, but this increased the number of book covers by 180%, since the services that do have an API aren&#8217;t as comprehensive.  So whatchagonnado.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-3.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-3.jpeg" alt="" width="699" height="1059" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112199" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-3.jpeg 699w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-3-198x300.jpeg 198w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-3-676x1024.jpeg 676w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 699px) 100vw, 699px" /></a></p>
<p>Covers are nice.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="115" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112200" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4.jpeg 1373w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4-300x41.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4-1024x141.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-4-768x106.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>I also added a new command to just list all the books in one big buffer:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="241" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112201" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5.jpeg 1378w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5-300x86.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5-1024x294.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-5-768x221.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Because I realised that having a buffer with authors, and then books by specific authors is all well and fine, but it&#8217;s really just much faster to <tt>C-s</tt> for a book name than to first find the author, and then find the book.  I mean, I&#8217;ve not got a million books; it&#8217;s just er:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-6.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-6.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="90" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-112202" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-6.jpeg 944w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-6-300x32.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-04-15-6-768x83.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>That many.</p>
<p>Hey, now I can get data out of this thing by just clicking on the columns&#8230;  Let&#8217;s see&#8230;  I&#8217;ve got 432 unread books!  Sure!  I&#8217;ll get to them all one day.</p>
<p>(Actually, looking over that list, it looks like I&#8217;ve forgotten to mark a large number of books as read&#8230;  uhm&#8230;  I&#8217;m guesstimating about 100?  I should revise the data one of these days.)</p>
<p>Anyway, the code is on <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/bookiez.el.git" data-cached-time="2025-04-15T16:44:06" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/cache-2025-04-15-web.webp" onmouseenter="hoverLink(event)">Microsoft Github</a>.  I&#8217;m not sure anybody would find this usable as is, but perhaps there&#8217;s some useful bits.  At least the <tt>isbn.el</tt> library in there is somewhat helpful.</p>
